{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And on the day of Shabbat.</b> In all the offerings the term הקרבה (offering) or עשיה (making) is written, but for Shabbat, since melakhah is forbidden on it because of its honor, the terms הקרבה and עשיה are not said concerning its offerings — as though no melakhah is performed in them." "<b>Two lambs.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, did not impose excessive burden in the musaf of Shabbat; rather, the musaf equals the tamid. And no חטאת is said in it, as in the other musaf offerings, because of the honor of Shabbat — for one may not slaughter on Shabbat anything eaten by any person; rather, all of its offering is לגבוה (for Heaven), and upon this they established 'you shall be pleased with the burnt offerings of Shabbat' (a phrase from liturgy). And even though musaf חטאת offerings are brought on it, such as on a Shabbat of Rosh Chodesh and a Shabbat of Yom Tov, nevertheless in the musaf of an ordinary Shabbat the Merciful One made a distinction." "<b>And its libation.</b> It refers to wine libations."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:05.008780798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}